    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d471">

                <pb facs="0689" n="679" xml:id="pg679"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Austria)/12–645:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the United States Political
                        Adviser for Austrian Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Erhardt</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-12-09T21:00:00-05:00">December 9, 1945—9
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>347. Reurtel 536.<anchor n="47" xml:id="d471-f1"/> Until political groups can be
                    carefully examined with reference to their objectives and composition Department
                    recommends that no action be taken. Following consultation with War Department,
                    instructions will be sent.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d471-f1" n="47" xml:id="d471-f1-content">
                <p>In this telegram of December 6, not printed, the Political Adviser reported that
                    for administrative reasons the Allied Council was considering waiving the
                    requirement that minor political parties submit their program to the Allied
                    Council before engaging in any political activity. All parties that conformed to
                    basic democratic principles would henceforth be free to operate without the
                    necessity of getting Allied Council approval. (740.00119 Control
                    (Austria)/12–645)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
